    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `fill_gaps` in `app/gaps.py`, and all 4 tests pass (2 existing, 2 I added).\n\n**How it works:**\n- It groups `temp_c` by station and fills each gap with that station's most recent earlier temperature. Gaps that are still empty then get the station's first later temperature. Existing values are never overwritten.\n- Values only come from the same station. A station with no temperatures at all keeps its gaps.\n- It works on a copy, so the input frame isn't changed. Row order, the index and the other columns come back exactly as they were.\n- It still lines rows up correctly if the index has duplicate labels or isn't sorted.\n- Rows with a missing `station` keep their original `temp_c`, since there's no station to fill from.\n\n**Tests:** I added `tests/test_gaps.py`. It checks the result on the sample CSV and on a harder hand-built frame with duplicate index labels, a station with no temperatures, and a row with no station. It also checks that an earlier value is used before a later one and that the input is left unchanged.\n\nNo dependencies were added."
